---
import { carreno } from '../data/carreno';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Arrow from '../components/Arrow.astro';
import VideoLesson from '../components/VideoLesson.astro';
import { accessed, resources, videoLessons } from '../data/resources';
---
<Layout title="Resources & references" description="Watch demonstrations from The Emily Post Institute and explore cited university dining-etiquette guides.">
  <section class="resource-introduction section-shell">
    <h1>Watch. Read.<br/><em>Feel prepared.</em></h1>
    <p>Carreño’s principles, clear demonstrations, and practical references for your next professional meal.</p>
  </section>
  <div class="resource-collection section-shell">
    <resource-index class="resource-index">
      <nav aria-labelledby="resource-index-heading"><h2 id="resource-index-heading">In this collection.</h2>
        <a href="#carreno-foundation"><span>Carreño</span><Arrow/></a>
        <a href="#watch"><span>Watch & learn</span><Arrow/></a>
        <a href="#educational-sources"><span>References</span><Arrow/></a>
        <a href="#resource-context"><span>Context & credits</span><Arrow/></a>
      </nav>
    </resource-index>
    <div class="resource-collection-body">
  <section class="carreno-feature" id="carreno-foundation" aria-labelledby="carreno-heading">
    <div class="carreno-book" aria-hidden="true"><span>Manuel Antonio<br/>Carreño</span><span>Urbanidad<br/><i>y buenas<br/>maneras.</i></span><span>Consideration at the table.</span></div>
    <div><h2 id="carreno-heading">The foundation.<br/>Read with context.</h2><p>Carreño is this guide’s principal historical reference. His <em>Compendio</em> connects dining conduct with consideration for others. Each chapter identifies the relevant section and its application today.</p><p>We use the 2016 digital edition published by the Biblioteca Nacional de Colombia. Citations refer to <em>Urbanidad</em>, not the separate text by Rufino Cuervo included in the same volume.</p><a class="text-link" href={carreno.url}>Read the verified edition<Arrow/></a><details class="carreno-context"><summary>How to read the historical guidance</summary><p>The work reflects nineteenth-century social hierarchies and gender expectations. Our English synthesis retains practical principles of consideration, while applying equal respect, cultural flexibility and individual needs. Current place settings and recruiting practices are supported separately by Emily Post and university sources.</p><p>{carreno.edition}</p></details></div>
  </section>
  <section class="watch-library" aria-labelledby="watch">
    <div class="library-heading"><h2 id="watch">Small details.<br/>See them in practice.</h2><p>Six demonstrations from The Emily Post Institute. Choose a lesson to begin.</p></div>
    <div class="watch-grid">{videoLessons.map((lesson,index)=><VideoLesson {...lesson} tone={index%2?'light':'dark'}/>)}</div>
    <p class="video-source-note">Publisher sources and video addresses checked November 4–5, 2026. Videos remain on YouTube; the accompanying diagrams are our own. The linked written lessons cover the same skills without requiring video playback.</p>
  </section>
  <div class="resources-layout">
    <section aria-labelledby="educational-sources"><h2 id="educational-sources">The reading behind the guide</h2><ol class="resource-list">{resources.map(resource=><li id={resource.id}><div><p class="resource-organization">{resource.organization}</p><h3><a href={resource.url}>{resource.title}<Arrow/></a></h3><p>{resource.note}</p></div><p class="source-date">{resource.id==='carreno'?'Digital book':resource.id==='vt'?'PDF guide':'Article'} ·<br/> Consulted {['carreno','formal'].includes(resource.id)?'November 7, 2026':accessed}</p></li>)}</ol></section>
    <aside class="resource-notes" id="resource-context"><h2>Consideration comes first.</h2><p>Etiquette is a way to be considerate, not a measure of someone’s worth. These resources describe common U.S. professional dining conventions. Practices vary by culture, venue, host, and individual needs.</p><p>When sources differ, the chapters identify the context rather than presenting every convention as a universal rule. Ask a host a considerate question when you are unsure.</p><a class="arizona-resource" href="https://career.arizona.edu/">For Arizona students<Arrow/><span>Student Engagement & Career Development</span></a>
      <details class="resource-credits"><summary>Image & design credits</summary><p>The opening dining-room image is an AI-generated editorial illustration of a fictional setting, rather than an actual University of Arizona event. The chapter studies, place-setting diagrams and video illustrations are original instructional graphics. The interactive geometry and written chapters provide the dining guidance.</p><p>The dining room, furniture, tableware, rendered stills, diagrams, and interface graphics were created for this project. The room uses Three.js with original geometry and material maps. Cormorant Garamond and Source Sans 3 are self-hosted; their font licenses are included in the project.</p></details>
    </aside>
  </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <script>
    class ResourceIndex extends HTMLElement {
      resize?: ResizeObserver;
      update = () => {
        let target = window.location.hash || '#carreno-foundation';
        const links = [...this.querySelectorAll<HTMLAnchorElement>('a[href^="#"]')];
        if (!links.some(link => link.hash === target)) {
          const fragment = document.getElementById(decodeURIComponent(target.slice(1)));
          if (fragment?.closest('.resource-list')) target = '#educational-sources';
        }
        links.forEach(link => { if(link.hash === target) link.setAttribute('aria-current','location'); else link.removeAttribute('aria-current'); });
      };
      connectedCallback() {
        this.update(); window.addEventListener('hashchange', this.update);
        this.resize=new ResizeObserver(([entry])=>document.documentElement.style.setProperty('--resource-index-height',`${entry.borderBoxSize[0]?.blockSize??entry.contentRect.height}px`));
        this.resize.observe(this);
      }
      disconnectedCallback() { window.removeEventListener('hashchange', this.update); this.resize?.disconnect(); }
    }
    if (!customElements.get('resource-index')) customElements.define('resource-index', ResourceIndex);
  </script>
</Layout>
